      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "## 2. Does the gate find the mistakes?\nOn day 2 the gate marks about 22% of the traffic as unfamiliar. If the idea is right, the detectors' mistakes should be concentrated there. They are: nearly every mistake of every model falls in the unfamiliar traffic, and that traffic is mostly a SYN flood that looks different from day 1, plus normal traffic that changed."
