    {
      "id": 100,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "transparent": true,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 28
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "## 3. The router, live\nEach connection takes one of three paths. **Familiar** traffic is answered by the day-1 model. **Unfamiliar traffic close to a pattern already labelled** copies that label from a memory. **Unfamiliar traffic with nothing similar in the memory** is answered by the random forest, and its true label is requested through Kafka. Nothing is retrained. Grey is the day-1 model alone; green is the same model with the router."
      }
    },
